I'd like to get together a spoiler file.  I know we already have one, and
a very nice one, but the spoilers I am thinking of are of a different
nature ... not so much the stats on everything (damages, probability of
hitting, & so on) but tricks and tips - the kind of stuff that gets
people ahead quickly and keeps them from dying prematurely.  Different
sections such as Stealing, Surviving Orc Packs, Using Tools would be
included, as well as just nifty ideas like
SPOILERS AHEAD

getting a very low armor class by giving gold to a priest and then
becoming a leprechaun and stealing it back.

Clever stuff, that is.  I've played way too much hack, and I want to get
some return on all those hours - perhaps by helping out new players who
get frustrated by dying way too quickly.

Mail the stuff to urbndv8@ucscb.ucsc.edu, and I will compile it and
post it every now and then, as well as adding my own contributions.

It might tickle the brains of those on the dev team, too.

Some of my contributions:

You don't need a pet to kill a unicorn.  A ring of conflict will do, of
course, and if you have double speed (or perhaps even 1.3 speed) you
can just stroll up and whack it to death.  But lacking these, all you
need is a pickaxe:  dig a pit and stand at a knight's-move to it,
and the critter will fall in sooner or later, and you can kill it at
leisure.  The pit trick will help if you want to lob jewels at it too.

Orc packs may be easier to deal with if you have a large boulder nearby.
Get some weapons or jewels under the boulder by throwing or putting them
there, and the orc pack will mill around the boulder like flies around
a garbage can, and won't by and large bother you much unless you come
too near.   At the very least it will slow them down.

If you have a tinning kit, poison resistance is easy to acquire: just tin
lots and lots of poisonous creatures and eat the tins.  Tinned poisonous
creatures won't poison you, but you can acquire poisonm resistance from
them.

and so forth, the list goes on and on.

btw, the person who said that a blessed luckstone will lose its blessing
when dropped was WRONG, wrong, wrong.  That is a LOADstone and you do
NOT want to pick it up!  Luckstones don't do that.   There is another
way to tell a loadstone:  when kicked, they do not go anywhere.  That
is not my discovery.

If you do not think that having another spoiler file is a good idea,
please feel free to post or write to that effect.  But I think we need
a spoiler file with 'hot tips' and not 20K of statistics.

